WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Upbeat music plays. There is no talking in this video.] Anatomical Terms of Movement

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[On screen] Flexion & Extension

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
[On screen] Extension: a movement that increases the angle between two body parts.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
[On screen] Flexion: a movement that decreases the angle between two body parts.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[He raises his straight arm forward and up, then lowers it.] Flexion, Extension

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
[He squats down, then stands back up.] Flexion, Extension

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.500
[He bends his knee to lift his foot behind him, then straightens it.] Flexion, Extension

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:57.000
[On screen] Abduction & Adduction

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
[On screen] Abduction: a movement away from the midline.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
[On screen] Adduction: a movement towards the midline.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:33.000
[He lifts his leg out to the side and brings it back, then moves his arms out from his sides and back in.] Abduction, Adduction

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:41.500
[He spreads his fingers apart, then brings them back together.] Abduction, Adduction

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.000
[On screen] Circumduction

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:54.000
[On screen] Circumduction: a conical movement of a limb extending from the joint at which the movement is controlled.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:05.900
[He draws circles in the air with his arm, then with his leg.] Circumduction
